# Astro Portfolio Rebuild Design

## Objective

Replace the single-file pixel portfolio with a recruiter-ready Astro and TypeScript site for graduate software-engineering applications. Preserve the avatar, dark palette, pixel borders, and playful micro-interactions while making the content readable, evidence-led, accessible, responsive, and fast.

## Information Architecture

- The homepage contains the graduate-software-engineer hero, featured case studies, evidence-linked capabilities, education and work timeline, and contact actions.
- Human Nutrition Unit, Recipe Application, and Road Sign Detection each receive a shareable case-study route.
- Memory Map remains a supporting project and links to its repository.
- The public resume is downloadable without exposing the mobile number.

## Content Rules

- Use only facts present in Anson's approved resume or verified public project material.
- Do not invent metrics, outcomes, responsibilities, screenshots, or implementation details.
- HNU emphasizes six-person sprint delivery, owned pages, Sanity integration, site-wide testing, and Render deployment.
- Recipe emphasizes Flask Blueprints, repository and service layers, swappable persistence, AJAX workflows, pagination, authentication, and 25+ tests.
- Road Sign uses a labelled conceptual pipeline diagram and has no source/demo link until genuine assets are supplied.

## Technical Design

- Astro static output, strict TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, npm lockfile, and GitHub Pages base path `/Personal-Website/`.
- Typed project content is the single source for cards, filters, case-study pages, metadata, and structured data.
- Client JavaScript is limited to the mobile menu, project filters, command palette, email copying, reveal enhancement, and decorative canvas.
- Content remains visible without JavaScript. Reduced-motion mode disables non-essential animation.
- No backend, CMS, analytics, cookies, or reconstructed demo is included in v1.

## Delivery

- Develop on `codex/astro-portfolio` while preserving the current site in Git history.
- Gate publication on static checks, unit tests, browser tests, accessibility checks, production build, PDF verification, and representative Lighthouse audits.
- Deploy to the existing `1-1dole/Personal-Website` GitHub Pages URL through GitHub Actions.
